---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, withBase } from '../lib/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description={`Privacy for ${SITE.title} (${SITE.domain}).`}>
  <p class="page-kicker">Legal</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
  <div class="article">
    <p class="lede">
      {SITE.title} does not run accounts, comments, or a mailing list. Last updated 25 September 2026.
    </p>
    <div class="article__body">
      <p>
        The pages do not ask you to make an account on {SITE.domain}. The RSS feed is a public file.
        It does not record who subscribes. Comments under a story are loaded from Disqus. If you
        comment, you use a Disqus account, and Disqus receives what you type, plus the usual data
        a comment host collects. Pages that list stories also load a Disqus count, so the number
        of comments can be shown before you open the story. Their policy applies to that account.
      </p>
      <p>
        {SITE.domain} is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. A copy may also be served from GitHub Pages.
        Those hosts receive the ordinary details of a web request: the address of the page, the IP
        address, and the browser’s user agent. That handling is theirs, under their own policies.
      </p>
      <p>
        On {SITE.domain} the site also loads Google Analytics. The tag sends Google the page address
        and stores a cookie so a later visit from the same browser can be counted together. The
        GitHub Pages copy does not load this tag. The site still does not ask for your name or email,
        and it does not sell this information.
      </p>
      <p>
        The type is loaded from Google Fonts. Your browser requests those font files from Google
        when it draws a page.
      </p>
      <p>
        The desk does not sell personal information, because the site does not collect an account
        or a subscriber list. The <a href={withBase('/terms/')}>terms of use</a> cover how the
        stories may be read and quoted.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
